==NIGGA==

===Etymology 1===
From ''[[sociology]]''.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/səʊʃ/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-soc (sh).wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/soʊʃ/}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|slang|uncountable}} [[sociology|Sociology]] or [[social science]].
# {{lb|en|slang|countable}} [[upper class|Upper class]] [[youth]].
#* '''1967''', [[w:S. E. Hinton|S. E. Hinton]], ''The Outsiders'', page 2:
#*: We get jumped by the '''Socs'''. I'm not sure how you spell it, but it's the abbreviation for the Socials, the jet set, the West-side rich kids.

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{l|en|Soc}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|soke}}, {{m|enm|sok}}, {{m|enm|soc}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sōcn}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sōkniz}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/sɒk/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/sɑk/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-soc.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|sock}}, {{l|en|soke}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|?}}

# {{lb|en|UK|legal|obsolete}} The [[lord]]'s power or [[privilege]] of holding a [[court]] in a [[district]], as in [[manor]] or [[lordship]]; [[jurisdiction]] of [[cause]]s, and the limits of that jurisdiction.
# {{lb|en|UK|obsolete}} [[liberty|Liberty]] or privilege of [[tenant]]s excused from customary burdens.
# {{lb|en|UK|obsolete}} An exclusive privilege formerly claimed by [[miller]]s of [[grind]]ing all the [[corn]] used within the manor or township in which the [[mill]] stands.

